001b[99Gthe\u001b[103Gverifier's\r\u001b[9C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m7\u001b[13G\u001b[38;5;231mw\u001b[15Grking files mid-run wo\u001b[38Gld\u001b[41Gm\u001b[43Gke the orchestrator\u001b[63Ga channel\u001b[73Gbetween \u001b[82Ghem.     \u001b[92G      \u001b[99G  \u001b[102G   \u001b[106G  \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf \u00a0Allowed by auto mode\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mBoth nodes are running and I won't inspect their intermediate work \u2014 reading the verifier's files mid-run would\u001b[115Gmake\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bme\u001b[6Ga channel between them. While they work, let me fix something I noticed in that timestamp.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mFound a rea\u001b[16Gerror in my own record, and it\u001b[47Gma\u001b[50Gters becaus\u001b[62G the brief asks\u001b[78Gspecifically for wall-clock\u001b[106Gcost.\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command\u2026\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf  $ cat >> AGENT_GRAPH_LOG.md <<'MARK'\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;246m## 2026-10-31 04:20 UTC \u2014 orchestrator \u2014 CORRECTION: the timestamps in this log have been wrong\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m**Every timestamp in this log after roughly 02:40 UTC is overstated, by up to 122 minutes.** Caught\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;246mwhen the dispatch banner printed a real `date -u` of **2026-10-31T\u2026\r\u001b[15C\u001b[2BChecking\u001b[25Gfilesystem traversal scope\u2026 \u00b7 3m 46s \u00b7 \u2193\u001b[66G14.3k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[33;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
