[489.39161, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[7G\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m119 +\u001b[14G\u001b[38;5;231mexploit; masking in time is the only route. A transfer function referenced to channel 1111 is not *b\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m  \u001b[10G +\u001b[38;5;231miased* by noise on the                                \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m1\u001b[9G0 \u001b[14G\u001b[22mbolometer output, so the estimate survives \u2014 but variance is inflated and coherence depressed.\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m121 \u001b[13G\u001b[22m **Report coherence per frequency; do not assume it.**\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m122 \u001b[22m - Frequency steps are 250 s and **250 / 10 = 25 exactly**, so the pulser arrives at an *identical\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;246m...\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 155 \u001b[22m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 156 \u001b[22m State these as not-applicable rather than passing or failing them:\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 157 \u001b[22m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m 156 -\u001b[38;5;231m- **No amplitude variation at fixed frequency.** The drive is constant (verified elsewhere: 0.1\u20130.2%  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m 157 -\u001b[38;5;231m  over 13 repeats). Measured force varies ~25% *across* frequency, which is the shaker and stinger    \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m 158 -\u001b[38;5;231m  response, not a drive change. **No linearity test and no quadratic-thermal-path test is possible    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m 159 -\u001b[38;5;231m  from this run.**                                                                                    \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 158 +\u001b[38;5;231m- **No amplitude variation at fixed frequency.** Each frequency occurs exactly once in this run, so   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 159 +\u001b[38;5;231m  **no linearity test and no quadratic-thermal-path test is possible from it.**                       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 160 +\u001b[38;5;231m- **The drive force is *not* smooth across frequency, and part of it may be instrumental.** Force RMS \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 161 +\u001b[38;5;231m  spans 365\u20131521 mV, a factor **4.16**, and contains two **step discontinuities**: **+71% between 5.4 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 162 +\u001b[38;5;231m  and 5.5 Hz** and **\u221232% between 7.4 and 7.5 Hz**. A one-step 71% jump cannot be smooth shaker and   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 163 +\u001b[38;5;231m  stinger response; a reference-channel range or amplifier gain change is at least as likely. Form    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 164 +\u001b[38;5;231m  every transfer function as a strict ratio to ch1111 **on the same step**, where such a change       \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u2026 5 more lin\u001b[19Gs \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf \u00a0Allowed by auto mode\u001b[39m\u001b[33;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
