[541.312894, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[99C\u001b[32B\u001b[38;5;246m9\u001b[39m\u001b[33;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[541.465467, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[8G\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m57\u001b[12G\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m 156 -\u001b[38;5;231m- **No amplitude variation at fixed frequency.** The drive is constant (verified elsewhere: 0.1\u20130.2%  \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m 157 -\u001b[38;5;231m  over 13 repeats). Measured force varies ~25% *across* frequency, which is the shaker and stinger    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m 158 -\u001b[38;5;231m  response, not a drive change. **No linearity test and no quadratic-thermal-path test is possible    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m 159 -\u001b[38;5;231m  from this run.**                                                                                    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 158 +\u001b[38;5;231m- **No amplitude variation at fixed frequency.** Each frequency occurs exactly once in this run, so   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 159 +\u001b[38;5;231m  **no linearity test and no quadratic-thermal-path test is possible from it.**                       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 160 +\u001b[38;5;231m- **The drive force is *not* smooth across frequency, and part of it may be instrumental.** Force RMS \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 161 +\u001b[38;5;231m  spans 365\u20131521 mV, a factor **4.16**, and contains two **step discontinuities**: **+71% between 5.4 \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m62\u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;231m \u001b[14Gand 5.5 Hz** and **\u221232% be\u001b[41Gween 7.4 and 7.5 Hz**. A\u001b[66Gon\u001b[69G-step 71% jump c\u001b[86Gnnot\u001b[91Gbe smooth shaker and\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m63\u001b[14G\u001b[38;5;231mstinger response; a\u001b[34Greference-ch\u001b[47Gnnel range or amplifier gain change is\u001b[86Ga\u001b[88G least\u001b[95Gas\u001b[98Glikely.\u001b[106GForm\r\u001b[8C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m4\u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;231m \u001b[14Gevery\u001b[20Gt\u001b[22Gansfer functio\u001b[37G as\u001b[41Ga strict \u001b[51Gatio to ch1111\u001b[66G**on the\u001b[75Gsame step**,\u001b[88Gwhere such a change  \u001b[110G   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;246m\u2026 5 more lines \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf \u00a0Allowed by auto mode\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mNow logging this episode \u2014 it's the most instructive one so far.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u001b[39m Running \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command\u2026\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf  $ T=$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ') && cat >> AGENT_GRAPH_LOG.md <<MARK\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;246m## $T \u2014 verifier \u2014 ATTEMPT 1 BLOCKED, and it caught two orchestrator errors anyway\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B**The most instructive episode of the pilot so far. Worth the prominence the brief asks for.**\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;246mThe verifier session exited 0 and printed \\`=== \u2026\r\u001b[14C\u001b[2BChecking\u001b[24Gfilesystem traversal scope\u2026 \u00b7 3m 48s \u00b7 \u2193\u001b[65G15.2k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[33;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[541.479511, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[17B\u001b[38;5;246m \r\u001b[6B\u001b[38;5;174m\u2722\u001b[39m\u001b[33;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[541.591796, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[17BLog the\u001b[11Gverifier episo\u001b[26Ge\u001b[28Gand\u001b[32Gfour\u001b[37Gerror\u001b[43Grows\r\u001b[6B\u001b[38;5;174m\u00b7\u001b[3G\u001b[38;5;180mEffecting\u2026\u001b[39m\u001b[33;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[541.65002, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[14C\u001b[23B\u001b[38;5;246m3m 48s \u00b7\u001b[24G\u2193\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m16.9k tokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
