[861.623929, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[1mP\u001b[5Gre waste:\u001b[22m verifier attempt 1 \u2014 produced\u001b[45Gn\u001b[47Gthing,\u001b[54Gcaused by my missing\u001b[75G\u001b[38;5;153mallow\u001b[39m list (E024). That's\u001b[101Ga\u001b[103Greal\u001b[108Gprocess\u001b[116Gcost\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Band\u001b[7Git\u001b[10Ggoes\u001b[15Gin\u001b[18Gthe\u001b[22Greport.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mMid-run:\u001b[22m ver\u001b[16Gfier attemp\u001b[28G 2\u001b[31Gis\u001b[34Glive\u001b[39Gand\u001b[43Galready\u001b[51Gwriting\u001b[59Gfiles\u001b[65G(\u001b[38;5;153mv01_steps.py\u001b[39m,\u001b[80G\u001b[38;5;153mVERIFIER_LOG.md\u001b[39m).\u001b[98GKilling\u001b[106Git\u001b[109Gto\u001b[112Grestart\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcheaper\u001b[11Grisks\u001b[17Ga\u001b[19Gthird\u001b[25Gattempt,\u001b[34Gwhich\u001b[40Gwould\u001b[46Gcost\u001b[51Gmore\u001b[56Gthan\u001b[61Gthe\u001b[65Gmodel\u001b[71Gdifference.\u001b[83GMy\u001b[86Grecommendation\u001b[101Gis\u001b[104Gto\u001b[107Glet\u001b[111Git\u001b[114Gfinish.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mStill to come:\u001b[22m critic, reconcile (me, no subagent), and \u2014\u001b[61Gmuch th\u001b[69G largest \u2014 Step 6, which is three more node runs.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BTwo honest observa\u001b[23Gons before you decide:\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B- \u001b[1mThe critic is the cheapest safe downgrade.\u001b[48G\u001b[22mIts\u001b[52Gchecks\u001b[59Gare\u001b[63Genumerable\u001b[74Gand\u001b[78Gnumeric:\u001b[87Gcausality,\u001b[98Gpositive\u001b[107Gdamping,\u001b[116GPT\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bcoincidence,\u001b[18Gcross-channel\u001b[32Gand\u001b[36Gcross-method\u001b[49Gconsistency,\u001b[62GSNR\u001b[66Gabove\u001b[72Gnoise\u001b[78Gfloor.\u001b[85GI\u001b[87Ghand\u001b[92Git\u001b[95Gthe\u001b[99Gthresholds;\u001b[111Git\u001b[114Greports\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gpass/fail with the number. But the caveat ma\u001b[50Gters \u2014 the critic exists to\u001b[78Gcatch subtle errors, and \u001b[1ma weak critic \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mthat passes everything is worse than no critic\u001b[22m, because it manufacture\u001b[76G fa\u001b[80Gse assur\u001b[90Gce. Mitigation: require\u001b[114Git to\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Brint the\u001b[15Gnumber behind every verdi\u001b[41Gt so I can audit its arithm\u001b[69Gt\u001b[71Gc instead of\u001b[84Gtrusting its judgment.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mT\u001b[7Ge model choice is \u001b[26Got the biggest lever; Step 6 is.\u001b[22m No model swap saves a\u001b[81G much as dropp\u001b[96Gng i\u001b[101G.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BAlso worth saying: a large share of the spend is my context. This conversation\u001b[82Gis long\u001b[90Gand every \u001b[101Gurn\u001b[105Gre-reads\u001b[114Git.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BI'll\u001b[8Gbatch\u001b[14Gtool\u001b[19Gcalls\u001b[25Gharder\u001b[32Gand\u001b[36Gstop\u001b[41Gprinting\u001b[50Glong\u001b[55Gtables.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u00a0\u001b[39mUser\u001b[8Ganswered Claude's questio\u001b[34Gs:\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf \u00a0\u00b7 Which model should the physics critic run on? \u2192 Sonnet, with audited numbers (Recommended)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;246m\u00b7 Given the usage concern, what should happen to Step 6? \u2192 Keep it, decide after stop point 4\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[6G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[33;1H\u001b[31;3H\u001b[?25h"]
