[877.134884, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mThe critic is the cheapest safe downgrade.\u001b[22m Its checks\u001b[59Gare enumerable and numeric: causality,\u001b[98Gpositive damping, PT\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  coincidence, cross-channel and cross-method consistency, SNR above noise floor. I hand it the thresh\u001b[106Glds;\u001b[114Greports\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bpass/fail\u001b[15Gwith\u001b[20Gthe\u001b[24Gnumber.\u001b[32GBut\u001b[36Gthe\u001b[40Gcaveat\u001b[47Gmatters\u001b[55G\u2014\u001b[57Gthe\u001b[61Gcritic\u001b[68Gexists\u001b[75Gto\u001b[78Gcatch\u001b[84Gsubtle\u001b[91Gerrors,\u001b[99Gand\u001b[103G\u001b[1ma weak critic \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m  \u001b[1mthat passes everything is worse than no critic\u001b[22m, because\u001b[61Git manufactur\u001b[76G false assurance.\u001b[94GMitigation: require it to\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bprint\u001b[11Gthe\u001b[15Gnumber\u001b[22Gbehind\u001b[29Gevery\u001b[35Gverdict\u001b[43Gso\u001b[46GI\u001b[48Gcan\u001b[52Gaudit\u001b[58Gits\u001b[62Garithmetic\u001b[73Ginstead\u001b[81Gof\u001b[84Gtrusting\u001b[93Gits\u001b[97Gjudgment.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mThe model choice is not the biggest lever; Step 6 is.\u001b[59G\u001b[22mNo\u001b[62Gmodel\u001b[68Gswap\u001b[73Gsaves\u001b[79Gas\u001b[82Gmuch\u001b[87Gas\u001b[90Gdropping\u001b[99Git.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2BAlso worth saying: a large share of the spend i\u001b[52Gmy \u001b[56Gontext. This conversation is long and every turn re-reads it.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BI'll batch tool calls \u001b[27Grd\u001b[30Gr\u001b[36Gst\u001b[39Gp printing long \u001b[56Gables.\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u25cf\u00a0\u001b[39mUser answered Claude's questions:\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf \u00a0\u00b7 Which model should the physics critic run on? \u2192 Sonnet, with audited numbers (Recommended)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5G \u001b[38;5;246m\u00b7 Given the usage concern, what sh