[880.022875, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1282 +\u001b[38;5;231mTwo points made honestly. First, the model choice is **not** the biggest lever \u2014 Step 6 is three more\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[5G \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1283 +\u001b[38;5;231mnode runs and dominates everything else. Second, a large share of the spend is the orchestrator's own\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1284 +\u001b[38;5;231mcontext: this conversation is long and each turn re-reads it, so tool calls will be batched harder   \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1285 +\u001b[38;5;231mand long tables kept out of the terminal.                                                            \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1286 +\u001b[38;5;231m                                                                                                     \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1287 +\u001b[38;5;231mRecommendation against killing verifier attempt 2 to restart it cheaper: it is mid-run and producing \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[5G \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1288 +\u001b[38;5;231mfiles, and a third attempt would cost more than the model difference.                                \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 1289 +\u001b[38;5;231m                                                                                                     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1290 +\u001b[38;5;231m**Decisions.**                                                                                       \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1291 +\u001b[38;5;231m                                                                                                     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 1292 +\u001b[38;5;231m1. **Critic on Sonnet, with its arithmetic audited.** The critic's checks are enumerable and numeric,\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1293 +\u001b[38;5;231m   so the orchestrator supplies every threshold and requires the number behind each pass/fail, and   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1294 +\u001b[38;5;231m   then re-checks the arithmetic itself. The stated risk, recorded because it is real: the critic is \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 1295 +\u001b[38;5;231m   the node whose purpose is catching what the other two missed, and **a weak critic that passes     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 1296 +\u001b[38;5;231m   everything is worse than no critic** because it manufactures false assurance. The audit requiremen\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m      +\u001b[38;5;231mt                                                                                                    \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1297 +\u001b[38;5;231m   is the mitigation, and it shifts the orchestrator from consumer to backstop for this node. Whether\r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1298 +\u001b[38;5;231m   that mitigation held is a question PROCESS_REPORT.md must answer rather than assume.              \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m 1299 +\u001b[38;5;231m2. **Step 6 kept, decision deferred to after stop point 4**, as Vivek previously directed. Steps 1-5 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 1300 +\u001b[38;5;231m   are delivered first.                                                                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 1301 +\u001b[38;5;231m                                                                                                     \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m 1302 +\u001b